FINAL VALIDATION CHECKS
- Output exactly the specified top-level keys; use empty arrays and null for missing information.
- Every component_id referenced in candidate_expected_answers and unresolved_ambiguities must exist in answer_requirements.
- Every evidence_id referenced anywhere must exist in evidence_items and in the incoming search_evidence_json; preserve IDs verbatim.
- Every retained evidence_items entry must correspond to a supplied input source; never invent a citation or source.
- A supported candidate expected answer requires directly relevant, sufficiently reliable evidence with matching scope and date; an MQU hypothesis alone cannot justify supported.
- If resolved_target.resolution_status='resolved', explain how the particular user visual referent was grounded, not merely why an entity exists on the web.
- Do not treat lack of conflicting search results as proof of truth. Preserve ambiguity when visual identity cannot be verified with available tools.
- Ensure coverage counts match answer_requirements and the supported candidate_expected_answers; multiple answers for one component count only once.
- No result-specific claims, MRU outputs, relevance/factuality scores, or fabricated certainty.
